<title>FRANCE: French unemployment up 39,500 in Aug, rate 12.6 pct.</title>
<headline>French unemployment up 39,500 in Aug, rate 12.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of people unemployed in France in August, adjusted for seasonal variations, rose 39,500 from July to 3,085,100, Labour Ministry data showed.</p>
<p>The jobless rate, based on International Labour Organisation (ILO) criteria, which exclude jobseekers who did any work, hit a record 12.6, up from 12.5 percent.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following seasonally adjusted data:</p>
<p>				  end-Aug   month-on-month year-on-year</p>
<p> Jobless rate (ILO)	 12.6 pct  +0.1 pctge pt  +1.0 pctge pt</p>
<p> Unemployment		3,085,100    +1.3 pct	   +5.3 pct</p>
<p> Unemployment (ILO)	3,220,000    +0.6 pct	   +9.1 pct</p>
<p> Jobs offered		  182,800    -3.9 pct	   +9.7 pct</p>
<p> New jobless registrations 375,700    -0.4 pct	   +2.0 pct</p>
<p> Jobless register exits    353,100    -4.3 pct	   +1.1 pct</p>
<p> Men under 25		  284,500    +2.4 pct	   +8.6 pct</p>
<p> Women under 25		323,300    -0.2 pct	   +2.4 pct</p>
<p> Men between 25 and 49   1,038,700    +2.1 pct	   +6.9 pct</p>
<p> Women between 25 and 49 1,065,700    +0.8 pct	   +2.8 pct</p>
<p> Men 50 and over	     213,000    +1.0 pct	   +8.0 pct</p>
<p> Women 50 and over	   159,900    +0.9 pct	   +9.5 pct</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5381</p>
